          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: Recent testimony (04/09/2014) of an old observation that the witness cannot recall the exact date (July 1st is arbitrarily assigned). A witness and his wife observe from a distance the unusual movements of a luminous phenomenon. No particular noise is heard during the observation, which lasts for 5 minutes. Only one testimony is collected. This observation of a white, luminous ball with irregular, erratic behavior is very strange. The only conceivable hypothesis, given the intense heat, would be a globular lightning phenomenon. Since the precise date is unknown and the old observation (over 30 years) makes a thorough investigation impossible, this strange case is classified \"C\" due to lack of information and cross-references.",
